ce-atlas) — AGENTS & Skills Studio: a full-page DSH panel to edit global and workspace AGENTS.md, manage project and global skills, and install skills from four public catalogs.\n\n- [chenkui-luo/awesome-dsh-submit](https://github.com/chenkui-luo/awesome-dsh-submit) — Skill that submits a DSH plugin repository to the awesome-dsh-plugin list: eligibility check, entry file, PR and CI result.\n- [feely0208/dsh-industry-hr](https://github.com/feely0208/dsh-industry-hr) — Recruiting-industry compliance check skill: resume personal data, discriminatory wording and background-check consent.\n- [feely0208/dsh-industry-manufacturing](https://github.com/feely0208/dsh-industry-manufacturing) — Manufacturing-site compliance checks: safety-training hours, special-equipment registration, product labeling and hazardous-chemicals handling.\n- [feely0208/dsh-industry-realestate](https://github.com/feely0208/dsh-industry-realestate) — Real-estate sales compliance checks: advertising promises, school-district wording, price display and pre-sale fund supervision.\n- [feely0208/dsh-industry-tax](https://github.com/feely0208/dsh-industry-tax) — Finance and tax compliance checks: invoice and voucher retention periods, tax-data export, invoice title and tax-ID validation.\n- [goodrain/rainskills](https://github.com/goodrain/rainskills) — Open-source agent skills that let Codex, Claude Code, Pi Agent, DeepSeek Harness, WorkBuddy and Hermes Agent deploy the current project to Rainbond, verify pages and APIs, troubleshoot, manage versions and roll back.\n- [xuelinzheng41-maker/dsh-academic-skills](https://github.com/xuelinzheng41-maker/dsh-academic-skills) — Unofficial DSH port of ARS academic-paper-reviewer (phase 1: reviewer only); CC BY-NC 4.0, non-commercial.\n\n- [bugtakue/ronge-skill-studio](https://github.com/bugtakue/ronge-skill-studio) — Ronge Skill Studio: context-aware skill recommendations, remote Discover/install, an MCP tools directory, default Plan/Immersive modes, experience memory with feedback, and a completion chime for DeepSeek Harness.\n- [shi004/better-search](https://github.com/shi004/better-search) — DeepSeek Harness skills for source-first web research with traceable evidence, plus a vendored browser-routing skill.\n- [1837620622/ad-and-psim-skill](https://github.com/1837620622/ad-and-psim-skill) — AI-driven Altium Designer & PSIM skills for editable circuit modeling, schematic layout and native simulation (proprietary commercial license).\n- [bugtakue/ronge-adaptive-skill-archive](https://github.com/bugtakue/ronge-adaptive-skill-archive) — Context-aware, self-evolving skill cockpit for DeepSeek Harness: recommendations with reasons, 10% exploration, live \"now using\", plan/immersive modes, experience memory, local safety scan, update diff/rollback (MIT).\n- [young-yyj/dsh-skill-browser](https://github.com/young-yyj/dsh-skill-browser) — Read-only local skill browser for DeepSeek Harness.\n- [tectivirus/cheng-yi-jing-skill](https://github.com/tectivirus/cheng-yi-jing-skill) — 程一镜 (Cheng Yijing), an industrialised short-drama skill for MiniMax H3 Ref2VA: turns a script into single-shot tasks that can be generated, edited and tracked.\n- [2842895276/dsh-skill-literature-reading](https://github.com/2842895276/dsh-skill-literature-reading) — Literature reading skill: classifies papers into core/related/method, adapts depth to your level, auto-archives PDFs and builds paper cards.\n- [mikuniemo/dsh-skill-router](https://github.com/mikuniemo/dsh-skill-router) — Cuts skill-directory cost from O(all skills) to about 600 tokens: a resident router plus on-demand category indexes; zero dependencies, cross-platform.\n- [Hongcheng-LI/dsh-paperwriter](https://github.com/Hongcheng-LI/dsh-paperwriter) — The Paperwriter skill packaged as a DSH plugin, with a dsh-market index.\n- [felix-lius/design-patent-views](https://github.com/felix-lius/design-patent-views) — Generate China design-patent drawings from STEP models: six orthographic views, a perspective view, JPEG submission files and editable DXF, fully local; ships a SKILL.md so a DSH agent can drive it.\n- [HaoyanZhang123/control-your-skills](https://github.com/HaoyanZhang123/control-your-skills) — A small personal set of DeepSeek Harness skills for Git release hygiene and repository presentation.\n- [modbusLV/dsh-academic-research-skills](https://github.com/modbusLV/dsh-academic-research-skills) — DeepSeek Harness adaptation of Academic Research Skills (ARS v3.24.0): research, write, integrity check, peer review and revise, packaged as native DSH skills (CC BY-NC 4.0).\n- [alitrack/dsh-gov-bp](https://github.com/alitrack/dsh-gov-bp) — Government-facing BP skills for DeepSeekRuntime: a seven-question review with a do-not-send threshold, the nine-chapter 试点申报 outline with policy-citation cards and a GB/T 9704 format layer, investor-to-application language conversion, and quoting built bottom-up from person-months (CSBMK 口径) with secrecy and copyright red lines. Zero dependencies.\n- [beiyanpiki/dsh-ulw-plan](https://github.com/beiyanpiki/dsh-ulw-plan) — omo explore → plan → execute workflow for DeepSeek Harness: `/ulw-plan` and `/ulw-execute`, four read-only role agents, inline task, and a plan-mode write guard.\n- [russeell/job-search](https://github.com/russeell/job-search) — Agent Skill that pulls jobs straight from company career sites and job platforms, with real posting dates and original application links; works in Claude Code, Codex and similar agents.\n\n## Resources\n\n- [jonestark12138/deepseek-harness-source-learning](https://github.com/jonestark12138/deepseek-harness-source-learning) — Chinese illustrated source-code tutorial for DeepSeek Harness: hand-drawn analogies explaining Agent Harness, TypeScript, monorepo, and Cordis.\n- [deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) — Official source repo.  `⭐38238`\n- [DeepSeek Harness overview (ai-bot.cn)](https://ai-bot.cn/deepseek-harness) — Third-party writeup.\n- [Finding the Best Harness for DeepSeek V4 Flash (Composio)](https://composio.dev/content/best-agent-harness-deepseek-v4-flash)\n- [flaqai/deepeseek-harness-guide](https://github.com/flaqai/deepeseek-harness-guide) — Guide for development with DeepSeek Harness; building a plugin for the DeepSeek Harness project.\n- [sandbaseai/deepseek-harness-handbook](https://github.com/sandbaseai/deepseek-harness-handbook) — Agent-first, multilingual handbook covering architecture, quickstarts, MCP, skills, subagents, sandboxing, and source-backed troubleshooting.\n- [zoahdev/dsh-tutorials](https://github.com/zoahdev/dsh-tutorials) — Bilingual tutorials for DeepSeek Harness: getting started, architecture, plugin development, and contributor roadmap.\n\n- [ljsysfurryACE/dsh-plugin-story](https://github.com/ljsysfurryACE/dsh-plugin-story) — Full technical article on the three plugins featured in the official DeepSeek Harness selection: memory / compression / active scheduling.\n- [wold9168/dotdsh](https://github.com/wold9168/dotdsh) — Personal DeepSeek Harness dotfiles (configuration reference).\n- [yangl326-Dylan/learning-dsh](https://github.com/yangl326-Dylan/learning-dsh) — Versioned bilingual (EN/ZH) source-code learning pages for DeepSeek Harness, served as a dsh plugin at /learning.\n\n\n- [hlxstc-create/challenge-project-methodology](https://github.com/hlxstc-create/challenge-project-methodology) — A battle-tested methodology for high-difficulty AI-agent projects: grading gates, evidence-driven verification & self-evolution. OpenClaw & DSH versions.\n- [zoahdev/dsh-docs](https://github.com/zoahdev/dsh-docs) — PR-ready documentation proposals for DeepSeek Harness: plugin publishing guide, package cookbook, troubleshooting — every command verified.\n\n- [OwenZhao9/inside-deepseek-harness](https://github.com/OwenZhao9/inside-deepseek-harness) — Inside DeepSeek Harness (《深入浅出 DeepSeek Harness》): 21 articles, ~77k words, screenshots and numbers from real runs.\n- [diguike/book-deepseek-harness](https://github.com/diguike/book-deepseek-harness) — 《一切皮插件》 — a close reading of DeepSeek Harness source, a mini implementation, and real plugin-development case studies. 21 chapters plus a runnable mini-dsh, all data measured firsthand.\n- [godcreator02/dsh-mechanics-lab](https://github.com/godcreator02/dsh-mechanics-lab) — Independent research project on DSH's plugin-system mechanics: a set of reproducible experiments, with the verdict written into each test case's docstring.\n- [DylanMerigaud/dsh-internals](https://github.com/DylanMerigaud/dsh-internals) — A source-level audit of DeepSeek Harness: where the docs and the code disagree. 270 machine-validated citations, pinned to v0.1.0-rc.7.\n- [vinokok/dsh-external-access-guide](https://github.com/vinokok/dsh-external-access-guide) — Remote VPS deployment guide for exposing DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web over HTTPS.\n\n- [warmsum/deepseek-harness-python-tutorial](https://github.com/warmsum/deepseek-harness-python-tutorial) — DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Python tutorial: a 17-chapter from-scratch implementation of the Agent Loop, plugin system, tool calling, Session, context engineering, Subagent, and Headless CLI.\n- [awesome-deepseekharness/deepseek-official-tracker](https://github.com/awesome-deepseekharness/deepseek-official-tracker) — DeepSeek official tracker across 6 sources (API changelog, API news, deepseek.com blog, GitHub releases, HuggingFace, npm dsh); auto-updated every 6h by GitHub Actions.\n- [Prism-Shadow/deepseek-harness-book](https://github.com/Prism-Shadow/deepseek-harness-book) — 《从零开始玩转 DeepSeek Harness》— a practical DeepSeek Harness field guide.\n- [PerryLink/dsh-plugin-guide](https://github.com/PerryLink/dsh-plugin-guide) — DSH plugin development knowledge base plus the dsh-plugin-dev CLI toolchain.\n- [ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-ci](https://github.com/ddtcorex/dsh-maestro-ci) — Reusable GitHub Actions workflows for Maestro/DSH plugin build and test jobs, package-entry checks, publish dry-runs, and npm/GitHub releases; CI infrastructure rather than a runtime plugin.\n- [siweimofang/dsh-plugin-zhishe-common](https://github.com/siweimofang/dsh-plugin-zhishe-common) — Shared JavaScript library for Zhishe DSH plugins, exposing JSON knowledge lookup, bundled reference-price matching, and heuristic risk labels; not a standalone DSH plugin.\n- [yyh-001/dsh-meme-packs](https://github.com/yyh-001/dsh-meme-packs) — Downloadable meme/sticker packs plus a machine-readable catalog for dsh-meme, published as GitHub Release assets so image bulk never enters Git history.\n- [ChenYu1991ppak/deepseek-harness-anatomy](https://github.com/ChenYu1991ppak/deepseek-harness-anatomy) — A progressive source-study tutorial of DeepSeek Harness (dsh): 17 chapters from a minimal agent-loop to multi-agent delegation, compaction, permissions and cross-process RPC, with runnable teaching code. Zh/En.\n- [benguinsan/bendo](https://github.com/benguinsan/bendo) — Personal-first todo app (Next.js / Clerk / Supabase) whose optional AI assistant runs on a self-hosted DeepSeek Harness overlay; the repository ships the `agent/doro` overlay as a template.\n- [holny/Agent-Harness-Develop-Book](https://github.com/holny/Agent-Harness-Develop-Book) — Agent Harness (Loop Engineering) development guide covering the complete architecture and core modules, based on production-grade agent source: Claude Code, DeepSeek Harness, OpenCode, Pi, Codex, OpenClaw and Hermes (English & Chinese).\n\n- [super-mortal/DeepSeekHarnessGuide](https://github.com/super-mortal/DeepSeekHarnessGuide) — DeepSeek Harness bluebook: a task-driven, plugin-first guide site (VitePress, 6 languages) taking you from a first working agent to a reusable work system.\n- [DeepSeek Harness CLI cheat sheet (dseek.app)](https://dseek.app/cli) — Unofficial third-party page: `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web` quickstart, Node.js requirement, headless and plugin commands, each linked to the official repo or npm page.\n\n- [Physicolor/dsh-design-resources](https://github.com/Physicolor/dsh-design-resources) — DeepSeek Design Resources — the interface spec, a reusable-source knowledge base and a live component gallery for DeepSeek Harness plugin authors.\n- [Ange4918/deepseek-code](https://github.com/Ange4918/deepseek-code) — Unofficial community guide to Deep Code CLI and DeepSeek Coder models: setup, usage and local deployment.\n\n- [BlanCatOra/dsh-plugin-standards](https://github.com/BlanCatOra/dsh-plugin-standards) — DSH plugin development standards: UI components, agent-facing repository docs, and a six-step pre-release process, all derived from real practice.\n- [huangye0623-creator/dsh-crash-avoidance](https://github.com/huangye0623-creator/dsh-crash-avoidance) — Postmortems of three real DeepSeek Harness incidents (Windows ACL/integrity, profile dependency duplication, preview API change), an upgrade regression checklist, and a multi-frame zstd log audit script. Unofficial.\n- [Cool-11/harness-competitor-eval](https://github.com/Cool-11/harness-competitor-eval) — Head-to-head harness evaluation of five AI agents (Codex / Workbuddy / DSH / Yuanbao Expert Mode / Doubao Office): three-layer attribution (model / skill / harness), a multi-question bank, full on-site records and reproducible reports.\n- [DeepSeekDSH](https://deepseekdsh.com/) — Free independent DeepSeek Harness guides — install, configure, plugins, MCP and troubleshooting, in English and Chinese.\n\n## Contributing\n\nPRs welcome! To add a plugin:\n\n1. Make sure your repo carries the **`#dsh`** GitHub topic.\n2. Add one entry under the most fitting category, format:\n   `- [Name](https://link) — Concise one-line description.`\n3. Keep the list alphabetical within each section where practical.\n4. One PR per logical change; keep descriptions factual and hype-free.\n\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for details.\n\n## Star History\n\n<img alt=\"Star History Chart\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dominic789654/awesome-deepseek-harness/main/assets/star-history.svg\" width=\"600\">\n\n<sub>Self-hosted chart, regenerated daily from this repo's own star count. GitHub\n[restricted the public stargazers API](https://github.blog/changelog/2026-06-30-upcoming-access-restrictions-to-public-api-endpoints-and-ui-views/)\non 2026-06-30, so third-party live charts (star-history.com and similar) no longer render for\nrepositories the chart service does not collaborate on. Data collection starts 2026-08-19.</sub>\n\n<!-- Previous third-party embed, kept for easy restore if GitHub reopens the API:\n<a href=\"https://star-history.com/#Dominic789654/awesome-deepseek-harness&Date\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://api.star-history.com/svg?repos=Dominic789654/awesome-deepseek-harness&type=Date&theme=dark\">\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://api.star-history.com/svg?repos=Dominic789654/awesome-deepseek-harness&type=Date\">\n    <img alt=\"Star History Chart\" src=\"https://api.star-history.com/svg?repos=Dominic789654/awesome-deepseek-harness&type=Date\" width=\"600\">\n  </picture>\n</a>\n-->\n\n## License\n\n[![CC0](https://licensebuttons.net/p/zero/1.0/88x31.png)](https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/)\n\nTo the extent possible under law, the contributors have waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights to this work.\n"
